From 827fd6c40efd64549b0e6f369e3edc939291b0eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivy Evans <ivy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:21:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Controller: the left stick walks a conversation's replies
 as the D-pad does

CSWGuiDialog keeps the reply index itself and answers only its own
previous and next events, which the module sends for the D-pad as the
direction codes; the stick's latched direction went to the focus layer,
which has nothing to move on that panel, so in a conversation the stick
did nothing while the D-pad worked (reported from play on a pad-only
device, 2026-10-15). In the dialogue input class the stick's latched
up or down is folded into the button word before the D-pad loop, with
the real D-pad taking precedence while held, so it gets the pad's press,
release and hold-repeat unchanged.
---
